.TH OPEN-IP-SCANNER 1 "July 2026" "Open IP Scanner @PROJECT_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
open-ip-scanner \- scan authorized IPv4 networks from a Qt desktop interface
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B open-ip-scanner
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Open IP Scanner
discovers devices on an IPv4 network selected by the user.
It presents results progressively and can enrich them with neighbor-cache,
hostname, vendor, and bounded service evidence.
.PP
Only scan networks and devices you are authorized to test.
.SH TARGETS
The Targets field accepts a single IPv4 address, an inclusive begin/end range,
CIDR notation, a shortened final-octet range, or a comma-separated combination.
At most 4096 distinct targets are accepted in one scan.
.PP
The Accuracy setting trades scan speed for retry depth and per-probe timeouts.
Stop requests cancel active work and preserve results already received.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/OpenIPScanner/OpenIPScanner.conf
Per-user settings when an XDG configuration directory is configured.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/OpenIPScanner/open-ip-scanner/diagnostics/
Optional diagnostic logs when local logging is enabled.
.SH NETWORK SERVICES
ICMP echo and the Linux neighbor table are used for discovery.
Enabled TCP service probes run only within the selected accuracy budget.
Hostname enrichment can use system DNS and the local Avahi mDNS daemon.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ping (8),
.BR ip-neighbour (8),
.BR avahi-daemon (8)
.SH REPORTING BUGS
Report issues at
.UR https://github.com/calculatetech/open-ip-scanner/issues
.UE .
